        <UserObject label="Grip span above optimum" tooltip="Grip span is the distance the hand closes around, from the back of the grip to the front. The sleeve alone is 56.9 mm (CAD estimate); with the squeeze trigger about 54–64 mm (CAD estimate). Both lie above the 45–55 mm span at which grip strength and comfort are highest.&#xa;&#xa;Source: ILO Encyclopaedia, hand tools" detail="Grip span is the distance the hand closes around, from the back of the grip to the front. The sleeve alone is 56.9 mm (CAD estimate); with the squeeze trigger about 54–64 mm (CAD estimate). Both lie above the 45–55 mm span at which grip strength and comfort are highest." source="ILO Encyclopaedia, hand tools" status="open" link="https://iloencyclopaedia.org/part-iv-66769/ergonomics-52353/item/634" id="n44">
