        <UserObject label="Deployment robot open: UR10e or H2" tooltip="Not yet decided between the UR10e and the Unitree H2 (possibly with a gripper on each hand); trade-offs not yet weighed. Known for the UR10e: a flange adapter plate (ISO 9409-1-50-4-M6) and very likely an external supply, since its tool connector provides 24 V at 2 A against the gripper&#39;s 3.5 A peak.&#xa;&#xa;Source: UR10e datasheet; Unitree product page" detail="Not yet decided between the UR10e and the Unitree H2 (possibly with a gripper on each hand); trade-offs not yet weighed. Known for the UR10e: a flange adapter plate (ISO 9409-1-50-4-M6) and very likely an external supply, since its tool connector provides 24 V at 2 A against the gripper&#39;s 3.5 A peak." source="UR10e datasheet; Unitree product page" status="open" link="https://www.universal-robots.com/manuals/latest/en/datasheets/ur10e/" id="n58">
